WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.450
At a Catholic funeral, a family gathers
in church to pray for someone they love.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.030
They pray for mercy, and for their
loved one to be at peace with God.

3
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.900
Catholics believe each person is judged
by Christ at the moment of death.

4
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:20.210
So if God judges everyone at death, why
do Catholics believe in a second judgement

5
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.840
at the end of time?

6
00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:26.590
In this mission, you'll map what
Catholics call the four last things.

7
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.580
Then you'll read a
puzzling line from Paul:

8
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.530
saved, but as through fire.

9
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:37.240
Your mission: find out why Catholics
believe in a second judgement at the end

10
00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.030
of time.
